def last_Digit_Factorial(n):
    # Base case: if n is 0 or 1, the last digit is 1
    if n == 0 or n == 1:
        return 1
    # Base case: if n is 2 or 3, the last digit is the same as the number itself
    elif n == 2 or n == 3:
        return n
    # If n is even, the last digit is 0 (since even factorials end with 0)
    elif n % 2 == 0:
        return 0
    else:
        # For odd n, the last digit is the same as the last digit of (n / 2)!
        return last_Digit_Factorial(n // 2)
```

