This Python function uses dynamic programming to find the longest common subsequence (LCS) of three string sequences. The function initializes a 3D list `dp` to store the lengths of the LCSs. It iterates through each character of the strings `str1`, `str2`, and `str3`, and updates the `dp` array accordingly. Finally, it returns the length of the LCS, which is found at `dp[str1.length()][str2.length()][str3.length()]`.

