def check(arr, n):
    i = 0
    k = 0

    # Check corner elements
    if arr[i] > arr[i+1]:
        i += 1

    if arr[i] > arr[i+1]:
        i += 1

    if i == n - 2:
        return True

    while i < n - 1:
        if arr[i] > arr[i+1]:
            k = i
            break
        i += 1

    # Find the next best element for k
    j = n - 1
    while j > k:
        if arr[j] > arr[k]:
            return True
        j -= 1

    return False
```

The solution employs the given approach to check if the array can be sorted by taking the first two and last two elements as corner elements. It uses two while loops to find the indices of the first occurrence of an element greater than its successor. If such an element is found, the function checks the remaining elements to find if they are sorted.

