This Python function `find_longest_conseq_subseq` will iterate through the given array `arr` of length `n`. It maintains two counters: one for the current consecutive subsequence length (`count`) and another for the maximum length of consecutive subsequence found (`max_count`). When it encounters two consecutive elements that are consecutive, it increments the `count`; otherwise, it resets the `count` to 1. The function updates `max_count` with the maximum value it has seen so far. Finally, the function returns `max_count`, which represents the length of the longest subsequence of consecutive integers in the input array.

